--- a/doc/usage/domains/python.rst
+++ b/doc/usage/domains/python.rst
@@ -58,6 +58,26 @@ declarations:
 
 The following directives are provided for module and class contents:
 
+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional ``canonical`` option gives the type
+   represented by the alias; it is parsed as a Python annotation and shown in
+   the signature after ``=``. A description may be included in the directive
+   body. Type aliases can be declared at module level or in a class, but the
+   directive cannot contain nested object declarations.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical: represented type
+      :type: Python annotation
+
+      Describe the type represented by the alias.
+
+.. rst:role:: py:type
+
+   Reference a type alias declared with :rst:dir:`py:type`. The role resolves
+   aliases in the same way as other Python-domain object references.
+
 .. rst:directive:: .. py:function:: name(parameters)
                    .. py:function:: name[type parameters](parameters)
 
